{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMomentScalingExclusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMomentScalingExclusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Monotone.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMomentScaling.clusterOrd_tendsto_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMomentScaling.clusterOrd_tendsto_zero","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMomentScalingExclusion.lean#L88-L96","doc":"The clusters tend to `0` as the body-order grows (`0 < r < 1`), so they\ncannot track an unbounded (growing) moment sequence: an explicit witness that\nthe exclusion is not vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMomentScaling.brunnian_identification_at_most_one_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMomentScaling.brunnian_identification_at_most_one_A","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMomentScalingExclusion.lean#L75-L86","doc":"**Structural exclusion (main statement).** If the Brunnian cluster order\n`c_A = κ·r^{A-1}` (`r = h² ∈ (0,1)`, `κ > 0`) is identified with a strictly\nincreasing residual-moment sequence `μ`, then the identification `c = μ` holds\nfor **at most one** body-order — hence it cannot be a magnitude closure for the\nwhole sequence. The clusters are strictly decreasing while the moments strictly\nincrease; they cross at most once. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMomentScaling.eq_at_most_once","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMomentScaling.eq_at_most_once","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMomentScalingExclusion.lean#L57-L73","doc":"**Cross-at-most-once.** A strictly antitone real sequence `f` and a strictly\nmonotone (increasing) real sequence `g` can agree at **at most one** index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMomentScaling.clusterOrd_strictAnti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMomentScaling.clusterOrd_strictAnti","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMomentScalingExclusion.lean#L39-L55","doc":"With `0 < r < 1` and `κ > 0`, the Brunnian cluster order is **strictly\nantitone** in the level index: co-present bonds are ever more `h`-suppressed, so\nthe cluster magnitude strictly decreases as the body-order `A` grows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMomentScaling.clusterOrd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BorromeanMomentScaling.clusterOrd","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BorromeanMomentScalingExclusion.lean#L34-L37","doc":"The order-normalized Brunnian cluster magnitude as a function of the level\nindex `k = A - 1`: `c(k) = κ · r^k` with `r = h² ∈ (0,1)` the per-order Hecke\nsuppression. (Working in `k` avoids `ℕ`-subtraction; `A ↦ A-1` is a bijection.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}